WEBVTT

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.260
We're going after Mister and his group!

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:15.380
All that matters is that they can still speak.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.490
Otherwise, do them the honor of a good smashing.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.140
Hokorimamire no bonnet

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.550
yubi de kyou o kizamu

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.020
Toori ame ga sugiru koro

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.850
ai no you ni kieta

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:04.090
Kokoro no naka nakusenu mono aru ka na

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:10.770
Mienai tsubasa habatakase

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:17.470
Koredemo katto fuku kaze ni mukaiuchi

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:24.710
Yuruginai kimochi de tachimukatteku no sa, go!

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:31.620
Sunabokori mau yakusoku no basho e

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:37.630
oretachi wa hashiritsuzukete yuku

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.750
Konya koso

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:44.270
Koete yaru

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:52.130
Ano saki made {no or ma???}

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:03.430
Episode 3

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:03.430
The One They Called "His Right-Hand Man"

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:06.420
Hell yeah!

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.660
Man, we've been waiting three years for this!

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:09.420
Right?

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.980
Don't you think it'd be better to hold off on the celebration until after we have the treasure?

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.690
Get outta here!

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.530
We made it this far, now we're as good as rich!

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:19.990
I don't know about that.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:20.920
Huh?

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:29.710
What, is there some kinda problem?

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:31.480
I'd say that's pretty evident.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:34.180
He's got it. Take a look behind us.

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:36.170
Huh? Behind us?

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:40.390
They're right on our tail!

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.890
Well, no shit!

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:42.960
So what do we do?

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.260
What we do is, well... y'know...

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.830
Run away.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.530
Do you mean you never even
gave this any thought?

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:54.870
Hey!

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:56.540
Sorry 'bout that.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.510
Get a grip!

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:01.310
Look, in any case we have the pendant.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:04.310
So we just shake 'em off and 
head straight for Graceland!

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:09.320
And lead them right to Pirate King Bruce's
legacy in the process?

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.920
What's your problem?

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.320
It's no big deal as long as we can shake 'em off!

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.290
And what if we can't shake them?

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.390
Hell if I know! Runnin's our only choice!

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:19.460
For crying out loud, you didn't do
squat planning this out!

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.330
You're the one who didn't do squat!

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.600
Pardon me, gentlemen.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:26.430
Our plans won't matter for squat anyway

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.240
if we have to spend a week digging up
all the din on Graceland.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:30.910
What's that supposed to mean?

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.810
Exactly what it sounded like.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:35.440
If we set foot on Graceland now,

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.250
we're not going to be finding any
legacy of Pirate King Bruce!

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.150
But we have the pendant...

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.850
And did you think there was, like, a map
hidden inside it or something?

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.590
Then what is that pendant for?

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:47.950
Let's put solving the riddle off until later.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:53.290
For now, we'll have to do something
about those dolls.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:58.300
Now then, how are we going to capture them alive?

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.770
I'm partial to hand-to-hand combat myself;

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:03.740
however, I'm just concerned that we may
end up ruining our clothes.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:07.210
That's right! This outfit was made just recently.

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:10.670
Oh my, and mine is brand new,
straight off the rack!

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:16.350
Do you think you could kindly leave someone
for us to pass the time with too?

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:19.920
If you want to join the party, then don't be late.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.820
That aside, does anyone know where May is now?

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:25.360
We still don't know.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.490
I see...

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:29.220
I'm sure she'll be fine.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.030
Here they come!

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.600
The party's starting, guys!

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.310
Now there's a line that takes me back!

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.040
It's like we've gone back to three years ago!

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.750
Shoot them to bits!

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.350
Without killing them, remember.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.820
I know.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:00.580
Damn...

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.290
They're getting carried away.

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:06.700
Can't you get 'em off our ass?!

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.070
Sorry, guys!

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:29.220
Taking the Coyote at full speed,
even along the moonwalk,

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.890
it will still take us three days to reach Graceland.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:34.100
After that, it will take us another half a day

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.830
to find Pirate King Bruce's legacy
and bring it back with us.

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:40.970
Bishop! How much time is left before they
drop the photonic bomb on Graceland?

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:44.340
Let's see... 5 days and just over 11 hours.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:48.440
5 days and 11 hours, minus 3 days
leaves us with 2 days.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:49.810
Well, that makes it simple.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:52.210
Okay then, we'll pull it off in two days!

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:54.480
So what are we going to do, exactly?

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:56.880
So you have a plan? Then tell us what it is!

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:57.720
<i>France!</i>

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.020
What?

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:01.320
Have you been in touch with Swamp lately?

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.920
Swamp?

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.330
Oh! You mean that Swamp?

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:09.260
The one they called Pirate King
Bruce Dockley's right-hand man.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:10.870
Swamp Gordon!

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:15.170
He and Bruce always operated together.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:20.970
That reminds me, you got into it
with him once, right, Bishop?

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:22.980
What, did you lose?

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.740
I haven't lost anything!

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:32.290
Do you know where Swamp is, Franca?

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:36.520
Swamp comes to drink at the
Pirate Hideout pretty often.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:38.150
He always asks me how I'm doing.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:43.930
He says to contact him if I'm ever in a bind.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.530
Connection made!

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:46.520
Huh?

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:48.900
Is there anything showing up on radar?

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.200
No, ma'am!

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:56.180
All right then! Time to head to Swamp's
for some tea and cookies!

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:57.510
Yeah, right!

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:59.780
It's not like you guys were anything like best buds.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.210
You guys know this story?

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:07.460
See, there was this small town
where no one ever got along.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:12.150
Some of the kids there were sick and tired of it,
so they put their heads together.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:15.930
They wondered if there was some kind
of situation they could cook up

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:18.800
that would force their hopeless parents
into cooperating with each other.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.900
And then suddenly, they had an idea:

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:24.140
They'd use an imaginary enemy.
Germs to be exact!

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:25.700
I mean, you can't see 'em, right?

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:28.910
Well, the plan was a great success.

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:34.410
The adults put the past behind them and scrambled
into action together against a common foe.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:38.490
So?

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:39.590
Jeez!

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:41.720
You bozos don't get it, do ya?

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:46.520
In our case, we don't even have to invent an enemy!
We've already got one!

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:49.660
Marciano!

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:52.430
So there you have it.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:56.590
Marciano...

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:10.910
Papa!

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:14.960
Target sighted!

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:16.080
All units reverse course!

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:22.390
Oh, c'mon! You mean after all the hide-and-seek
we're going to play tag again?!

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:25.230
Lead the dolls along like this,

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:27.530
and we'll bring 'em up right in front of Swamp.

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:30.370
Can you do it?

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:32.670
Hey, who do you think you're talking to?

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:34.970
This is Master Katana's
Super High Speed Express, man!

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:39.270
Let's focus on another happy day
and spend this time happily!

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:42.740
Think about what you long to do
from the bottom of your heart!

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:44.990
The future and memories of the past
are all we've got!

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.820
And between them we live!

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:50.190
We live! We live! We LIVE!

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:53.090
Food's so good to eat!

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:53.230
<i>Oh yeah!</i>

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:56.460
Thank you, O Sun!

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.470
And water's so good to drink!

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.570
<i>Oh yeah!</i>

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:04.130
Thank you, O Lord!

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:11.110
Show your gratitude to all living things!

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:11.310
<i>Oh yeah!</i>

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:12.250
Thank you!

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:14.780
There's nothin' to worry about!

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:15.920
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.420
There's nothin' to be down about!

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:19.610
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:23.220
Enjoy being alive!

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:26.250
The winners are the ones who enjoyed it!

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:30.230
Happy! HAPPY!

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.970
I'm beggin' you, Swamp.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.550
Happy all the time!

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:33.530
Come aboard!

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:37.940
Happy! HAPPY!

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:39.930
Happy every day!

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:49.720
It's been a full two days since he 
broke out of Sandvil Penitentiary.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:51.820
He oughta be showing up any time now.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:53.550
Boss Swamp...

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:55.160
What?

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:58.960
Would you say that Bruce's legacy
will end up going to Mister?

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.860
Don't you call him "Mister"!

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:03.400
Call him John or Jimmy, those are fine.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:07.340
Just hearing that name, "Mister", pisses me off!

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:08.740
Sorry about that...

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:10.400
But y'know, Boss...

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:13.370
It's not that we want the inheritance
ourselves, we're cool,

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:16.710
but aren't you the one who was
Bruce's number one man?

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:18.680
So if it's not you, but Mister...

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.550
I mean, John, who's gonna be the heir...

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.450
Franca is the heir.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:23.780
Well, yeah, that's true enough.

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:26.590
What was Bruce thinking when he gave Mister...

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:29.190
Don't you dare speak ill of Bruce!

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.790
Sorry!

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:34.790
Well, in any case the pendant isn't going
to be of any use on its own.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:36.930
Flying object confirmed on radar!

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:37.830
They're here?

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:39.030
They're headed our way!

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.940
All right, when they get within a range of 110,
throw everything we've got at 'em!

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:43.370
You sure that's all right?

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:47.980
If they're heading towards us,
there's a big chance Franca's aboard!

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.110
I know that.

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:50.440
So don't hit them.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:52.280
This is only to threaten them.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:56.880
Hey, Bruce, the man you chose has come.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:01.980
I'm gonna see with my own eyes
why you chose him over me.

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:05.520
They've gone into the hills in Altana.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:07.830
There are ten more units.

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.230
They're Guild helicopters!

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:11.070
Marciano?!

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:12.230
Fire!

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:13.720
Kill 'em!

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.040
Those are Bruce's enemies!

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.770
Marciano's Twelve Sisters!

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:21.830
March!

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:23.840
What's that?!

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:25.010
Hey!

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:26.540
Swamp!

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:27.670
Connection made!

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.120
Right on cue.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:31.080
Don't let the copters into town!

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:34.380
Shoot them down! Get 'em!

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:51.700
Let's at least take it easy while
we're on board the ship.

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:57.410
Even if we are in a hurry, it's not gonna make
this ship get to Ku-Rong any quicker.

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:01.740
What's the matter?

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:13.830
<i>It has been two days since the plan to attack
Graceland with a photonic bomb was announced.</i>

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:18.210
<i>Protests against the use of the photonic bomb 
are being made in various places throughout space.</i>

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.460
Captain!

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:17.430
Quickly...

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:20.230
Please fly this ship to Ku-Rong more quickly!

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:23.380
<i>We now take you to Sunflower, the capital of Manassas, which is the planet closest to Graceland.</i>

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:22.680
Marciano's Twelve Sisters have appeared on Ku-Rong

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:26.910
at exactly the same time that 
Marciano has launched her rebellion!

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.570
<i>This is Paris McCoy with ADN.</i>

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:29.810
<i>I am now in Sunflower, which is the capital of Manassas,
the planet closest to Graceland.</i>

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:29.600
It's fishy. It's all too fishy!

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:31.610
Now listen, Angelica...

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:33.520
<i>On this planet, over which there is the greatest
concern of potential after-effects from a photonic detonation...</i>

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:33.410
Look, just hurry!

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:38.620
What's the matter?

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:40.210
Angelica!

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:46.690
Tell me. What's going on?

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:48.300
Marciano starts a rebellion,

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:55.130
and then her elite task force, the Twelve Sisters,
show up on Sandvil then Ku-Rong.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:13:00.400
Why? Why have they gone after Mister?
You ought to know the answer to that.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.450
Sounds bad...

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:12.060
<i>Also, the Federation has announced in a press release...</i>

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:14.770
They've started the damn countdown for real.

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:15.270
<i>the identity of the man responsible for the plan to drop the photonic bomb.</i>

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:18.330
<i>Chief of Staff, Malcolm Lloyd, age 42.</i>

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:21.160
<i>At the age of 29, he was the youngest ever
to be promoted to the rank of General.</i>

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.700
<i>He was appointed Chief of Staff at age 38,</i>

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:28.640
<i>and has since been known by those around him
as a man who possesses an iron will.</i>

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:31.810
<i>Mr. Lloyd is already aboard the DK-9981 shuttle</i>

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:34.370
Doesn't exactly strike you <i>as</i> the flexible type, does he?

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:33.770
<i>loaded with the photon annihilation bomb,</i>

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:36.750
<i>and it seems he will accompany it to the drop point.</i>

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:36.810
Damn it!

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:41.000
I wonder if we could get them to put off dropping the bomb by putting him out of commission somehow'?

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:40.340
<i>No information pertaining to 
the drop point itself has been released.</i>

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:43.710
You mean like the way I did to
you once upon a time?

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:44.990
What'd you say?!

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:47.760
I'll pay you back ten times over
for that now if you like!

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:49.060
So you did lose.

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:50.220
Shut it!

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:53.760
Go for it, Hotshot. There is a reason you
came to see me after all, right?

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:55.500
So you gonna whack me then?

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.430
Go on, I'd like to see you try!

00:13:57.430 --> 00:13:58.690
Here, go on!

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:00.730
Don't even touch him.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:01.770
Shut the hell up!

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:03.970
Hey now, we haven't seen each
other for a long time.

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:06.170
How about you put out some tea
for us or something?

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:09.540
See, we're all pooped after spending the
whole night playing with the dolls.

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:12.480
You're as amusing as ever.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:13.650
Aren't I?

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:16.150
I did try turning over a new leaf
back in the slammer,

00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:19.880
but once a guy passes thirty,
it ain't so easy to change anymore.

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:24.460
You sure you can afford to be acting so laid back?

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.690
I thought you didn't have any time.

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:28.730
How about you try begging me?

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:33.460
Say, "Please, Mr. Swamp, sir, tell me the secret
of the inheritance that Bruce left behind!"

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:37.200
I know the significance of the pendant,
if that's what you mean...

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:38.470
Bud.

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:48.350
Whoa, that was too close.
You almost had me there.

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:49.750
You sayin' I'm lying'?

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:52.550
Then what did you come here for?

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:55.150
Being so short on time and all?

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:01.670
See? You can't even answer...

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.170
-It's Bruce's eye!

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:06.770
The secret of the pendant lies in Bruce's fake eye.

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:09.670
Whatever Bruce saw is all in there,
just like he saw it.

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:12.010
You knew'?

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:13.740
Yup...

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:20.750
Okay, you know the significance of the pendant,
so what did you come here for?

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:23.450
Was it to make a fool of me or something?

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:25.050
It was for you.

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:25.890
What?

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:28.820
I came here to ask Swamp Gordon,
Pirate King Bruce's number one man,

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:31.620
to take pan in this operation.

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:33.780
So sorry.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:36.560
There's no smoking here, you see.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:38.730
Huh? Oh, right...

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.430
Whoa, hold on.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:42.800
If you know the secret of the pendant,

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:46.010
then let's get the heck over to Graceland on our own!

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:49.810
You'd never accept such a ridiculous
request, right Boss?

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:51.610
Come on, you speak up too!

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:54.980
Doesn't matter to me if Mister wants
to go as a group of four.

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:56.550
Why you!

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:59.350
Just because we know the
secret of Bruce's pendant,

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:02.720
doesn't mean we'll be able to
get our hands on his legacy.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:04.960
The only one who will claim Bruce's treasure

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:09.530
is someone who has the same,
if not greater, power than Bruce.

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:11.590
Isn't that right, Swamp?

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:16.230
Good morning!

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:25.410
Ah, what a pleasant surprise, ladies!
Why, good morning!

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:27.680
Who are these people? Friends of yours?

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:29.620
Well, yes, I suppose you could say that.

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:31.890
Oh my, how wonderful!

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:35.990
This town is so very much in your debt, Mr. Swamp.

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:36.490
Isn't that right?

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:37.420
Yes!
Isn't that right?

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.360
This is perfect timing now that your friends are here.

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:42.960
The tomatoes Belinda brought today are fabulous!

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:44.430
Ripened to perfection!

00:16:44.430 --> 00:16:46.830
Cathy has some homemade cheese and bacon,

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:49.470
and there are also vegetables picked
fresh from Jane's farm.

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:51.540
So you all eat up, now!

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:52.770
Eat up, now!

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:55.440
Thank you for always going to
so much trouble for me.

00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:57.140
Thank you very much.

00:16:57.140 --> 00:16:59.180
Well, see you again tomorrow, Mr. Swamp.

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:03.670
We'll be looking forward to the next service too!

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:05.290
You're kinda...

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.480
...fawned over, aren't ya?

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:14.330
Let's have some breakfast!

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:17.520
Look, these tomatoes are glistening!

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:21.310
These won't need any kind of dressing at all, huh?

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:24.100
Okay, I'm gonna heat up the bacon,
so you take care of washing.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:25.770
Okay!

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:27.570
What should I do?

00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:29.540
Help me out here, Katana.

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:30.700
Gotcha!

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.110
Hey, you guys!

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:33.340
Yessir!

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:42.020
What are you being a minister for?

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:43.750
Talk about shady...

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:49.730
When you were a kid, didn't you ever write about
what you wanted to be in the future?

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:51.370
No way!

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:54.200
There's never "no way."

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:56.040
I don't believe it...

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:57.700
Tell me, Bishop...

00:17:57.700 --> 00:18:00.840
What would you write now?

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:02.380
Now? You mean, like, right now?

00:18:02.380 --> 00:18:04.380
Yeah, now.

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:06.510
Well, that's a no-brainer, isn't it?

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:09.010
I came here to do exactly that.

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:21.520
I'm going to leave the vegetables I washed here.

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:30.940
Let me say this first:

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:35.400
This doesn't mean I recognize you as Bruce's heir.

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:39.980
Now, how about you fill me in
on just what your plan is?

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:42.380
My plan?

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:45.820
I want to take Franca there.

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:50.880
I saw Franca working the bar while
you were in the slammer.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:55.560
Look, what I want to do is give that
inheritance over to Franca.

00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:58.330
That doesn't mean letting you get a hold of it.

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:00.430
Do you want money?

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:02.270
Wrong!

00:19:02.270 --> 00:19:07.110
It's been three years since Franca came
along with me. She's grown.

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:11.480
It doesn't mean I recognize you as the heir!

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:16.180
I want to find out now why Bruce chose you.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:18.280
How do you want to do that?

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:22.820
So how was Franca when she was at the bar?

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:26.260
She looked like she enjoyed it.

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:27.690
I see.

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:32.370
Was quitting the pirating business and
opening the bar all for Franca?

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:35.340
I wanted to be there for her.

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:37.770
I hope you're still a good shot.

00:19:37.770 --> 00:19:39.800
You better not miss.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:42.900
Same to you.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:03.590
What are you doing?
Don't just stand there!

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:06.070
Here you go, eat up!

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:03.220
Boss!

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:09.560
I'll be back in a week.
Give my regards to everyone, all right?

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:22.070
Swamp!

00:21:23.410 --> 00:21:25.480
What, so you came?

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:29.750
Well, we're going to have to repair the church,
y'know. It's all cuz of you guys.

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:30.880
Now shake 'em off.

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:32.090
Gotcha.

00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:33.380
And you.

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:38.230
I'm gonna see with my own eyes whether
you're the man to inherit Bruce's legacy!

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:41.630
Ah, shut up. Lemme enjoy this cigar in peace.

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:49.270
Time to repent!

00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:03.050
Is that so?

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:06.590
Mister and Swamp have gone into space together?

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:09.060
<i>Mother...</i>

00:22:09.060 --> 00:22:12.080
<i>Sep... Sep is dead.</i>

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:16.490
I believe I shall also go into space.

00:22:20.200 --> 00:22:24.810
You know that story about how the kids made up
some bacteria as a common foe?

00:22:24.810 --> 00:22:27.370
It's really been bugging me.

00:22:27.370 --> 00:22:29.310
Where did you say that all happened?

00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:30.980
Oh, that?

00:22:30.980 --> 00:22:33.370
That was just some story I read
and got a kick out of.

00:22:40.340 --> 00:22:43.880
<i>Hoho o tsutawaru</i>

00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:53.720
<i>shizuku doko kara kuru no</i>

00:22:54.840 --> 00:23:00.270
<i>Oshiete...</i>

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:05.070
<i>Makimodosenai</i>

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:12.650
<i>jikan to iu ruuru ni</i>

00:23:12.650 --> 00:23:20.060
<i>munagura tsukanda</i>

00:23:20.060 --> 00:23:23.800
<i>Koko ni aru "omoi" de sae</i>

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:27.220
<i>usuragu kioku ni</i>

00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:34.440
<i>teikou suru keredo</i>

00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:37.940
<i>Kitto koroshi ni kuru</i>

00:23:37.940 --> 00:23:44.550
<i>Sugite kita hibi no naka de</i>

00:23:44.550 --> 00:23:53.030
<i>Tatta hitotsu shinjirareru</i>

00:23:53.030 --> 00:23:59.370
<i>Koe o karasete naita</i>

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:02.700
<i>Koko e kite</i>

00:24:02.700 --> 00:24:06.370
<i>Soba ni ite</i>

00:24:06.370 --> 00:24:10.000
<i>Nee</i>
